refactor: one runtime dependency, three entries

The bundle only requires `css-render`, `react`, `react-dom` and the DSH
primitives. The rest (`anser`, `clsx`, `shiki`, `@shikijs/langs`,
`simple-icons`) were only ever needed because the primitives prebundle imports
them at module scope, which the host resolves for us, so they move to
devDependencies where the test and gallery builds can still see them. A plugin
now installs one package and nothing else.

The document baseline also stops being part of the component surface:

- `dsh-components` exports components and their prop types only
- `dsh-components/provider` exports `DshProvider`
- `dsh-components/styles` exports `installDshTheme`, `setDshDarkMode` and the
  token sheets

Importing a Button no longer pulls the token sheets or the theme installer into
the module graph, and a consumer that never renders outside DSH never loads
either entry.